# Quality Gates
# Scope: file/function/class size limits, coverage minimums, security (pickle, credentials).
# For linting tool config (E501, basedpyright), see quality-gates-hardening.mdc.
RULE: File 900 lines max; function 200; class 900; method 50. Coverage: MIN_COVERAGE = max(floor, actual-1) where floor=70% service / 80% library. No pickle; no credentials in repo.
WHY: Template enforces consistency; security violations are BLOCKING. Floor prevents repos falling below minimum; -1 allows one point of natural churn without regression alarms.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md §Coverage by repo type
DO: Use joblib/JSON/Parquet not pickle; *credentials*.json in gitignore; run via quickmerge (see always-use-quickmerge.mdc); recalibrate with `python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-unified.py --recalibrate`
NEVER: pickle.loads; commit credential JSON; exceed file/function limits without split; set MIN_COVERAGE below floor (70 service / 80 library) without QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md entry
See also: quality-gates-hardening.mdc (E501, basedpyright tool config); testing/test-coverage-targets.mdc (per-repo targets table)
